# The Cabin by the Lake install lives in `_game/` -- the whole Ren'Py
# distribution, moved there in one piece so the launcher still finds `game/`
# beside it. That is 2.1 GB of the author's assets and the Ren'Py runtime, and
# none of it belongs in a walkthrough repo. GitHub refuses a push over 2 GB, so
# committing it by accident fails slowly and confusingly.
#
# Hence deny-by-default: ignore everything at the root, then name the few paths
# the atlas owns. Anything that appears later -- a save folder, an updater's
# scratch files, a second copy of the game for a new version -- is ignored
# without anyone having to think about it.

/*

# ---- what the atlas owns ----
!/.gitignore
!/CLAUDE.md
!/README.md
!/_tools/

# The built app. Both are generated by `python _tools/make_app.py`, and tracked
# anyway because they are the deliverable: GitHub Pages serves the committed
# file, and nothing in this repo can rebuild it -- the pipeline reads
# `_game/game/`, which is the one thing that must never be in here.
#   index.html         the whole document, and what Pages serves
#   walkthrough.html   the same app as an Artifact fragment, with no doctype or
#                      <head> of its own because the Artifact host supplies them
!/index.html
!/walkthrough.html

# ---- generated inside the paths above ----
# `template.html` is written by make_template.py from _head.html + _app.js, and
# CLAUDE.md says never to edit it; tracking it would invite exactly that.
/_tools/template.html
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# ---- redundant under `/*`, listed so they read as deliberate ----
# `_game/` is the game. `_decompiled/` is its script, decompiled. `_analysis/`
# is the generated JSON plus the screenshots and probe pages the tools drop
# there. All three regenerate from `_game/` in a few seconds.
/_game/
/_decompiled/
/_analysis/
/_shots/
*.png
*.jpg
*.webp

# editors / OS
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
